# Target C — gapwise local-slack payment in the sharp wrapping window

**Date:** 2026-09-12  
**Base:** `f5d8c7997da0f3c63adf1977a45e96648773014e`, state `2026-09-12.audit.46`  
**Status:** proof-only Type-II candidate; theorem-state authority unchanged.  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** **STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.**

This note adds one source-level inequality to the endpoint ledger.  The local
internal-rhombus area/slack theorem is summed over each macroscopic harmonic-cell
group, rather than applied only to the wrapping carrier.  The complement-gap theorem
supplies an independent diameter floor for each group.  Together they give a second
positive payment for the large principal gap.

The dependency chain is

```text
Type-II gap area saturation + local area/slack
  -> S_j+G_j >= C_loc sqrt(A_j)
gap-spanning cell
  -> S_j >= sin(g_j/2)
all groups + Section 161
  -> stronger weighted diameter/topology inequality.
```

It is still a tradeoff.  It does not produce a strict sub-`D` source or close C-II.

## 1. Group inequality

For a finite disjoint family of macroscopic harmonic-cell groups `J`, write

\[
 S_j:=\sum_{r\in j}d_r,
 \qquad
 G_j:=\sum_{r\in j}(r_r+\eta_r),
 \qquad
 A_j:=\sum_{r\in j}A_{4,r}^{\rm int}.
\]

Here `A_{4,r}^{int}` is the unloaded-only strict-rhombus area in component `r`,
`d_r` is its attachment-cell diameter, and `r_r,eta_r` are the nonnegative
Section-160 remainder terms.  Let `a_j` be a normalized area lower bound:

\[
 A_j\ge(a_j-o(1))D^2.
\]

Put

\[
 a_0=\frac{\sqrt3}{2},
 \qquad
 C_{\rm loc}:=\frac45\sqrt\pi+\frac{2}{5\sqrt{a_0}}
 =1.8477910534538295\ldots .
\]

The finite local boundary argument gives, for every component,

\[
 \delta_r+r_r
 \ge \frac25 k_r+\frac25\sqrt{R_r},
 \qquad
 k_r\ge2\sqrt{\pi A_{4,r}^{\rm int}}-2\pi.
\]

Summing over a group, using `c_I=O(D^{2/3})`,
`A_{4,r}^{int}=a_0R_r+O(D)`, and
`\sum_r\sqrt{R_r}\ge\sqrt{\sum_rR_r}`, gives

\[
 \sum_{r\in j}(\delta_r+r_r)
 \ge C_{\rm loc}\sqrt{a_j}\,D-o(D).
\]

Since `eta_r=delta_r+2-d_r`, the group charges obey

\[
 \boxed{S_j+G_j\ge C_{\rm loc}\sqrt{a_j}\,D-o(D).}
 \tag{GLS.1}
\]

This summation is valid for all components in the selected group: the constant
`-4pi/5` per component is `o(D)` because the canonical number of positive-contact
components is `O(D^{2/3})`.  No per-cell convergence rate is assumed.

Suppose in addition that the same group has a gap or carrier diameter floor

\[
 S_j\ge(\lambda_j-o(1))D.
\tag{GLS.2}
\]

The two elementary lower bounds

\[
 3S_j+2G_j\ge3\lambda_jD-o(D),
 \qquad
 3S_j+2G_j=S_j+2(S_j+G_j)
 \ge(\lambda_j+2C_{\rm loc}\sqrt{a_j})D-o(D)
\]

therefore combine to

\[
 \boxed{
 3S_j+2G_j
 \ge
 \left[3\lambda_j
 +2\bigl(C_{\rm loc}\sqrt{a_j}-\lambda_j\bigr)_+
 \right]D-o(D).
 }
 \tag{GLS.3}
\]

The positive-part is important.  A thin small-area gap cell need not give positive
remainder by itself; (GLS.3) uses only the diameter floor and the aggregate local
inequality.

## 2. Endpoint specialization

Use the normalized Section-118 sharp-window constants from Sections 130 and 150:

\[
 \theta_*=2.704779235215494\ldots,
 \quad
 \phi_*=2\pi-2\theta_*=0.873626836748598\ldots,
 \quad
 \sigma_*=0.0088,
\]

\[
 g_1=\theta_*-\frac{10}{3}\sigma_*
 =2.675445901882161\ldots,
\quad
 \mu_*=\sin(\theta_*/2)=0.9762439137425688\ldots .
\]

Take four disjoint groups: the wrapping carrier `w` and the three principal gap
groups.  Their conservative area floors and diameter floors are

\[
\begin{array}{c|c|c}
 j & a_j & \lambda_j\\ \hline
 w & 0.4703752868004241 & \mu_*\\
 1 & G(g_1) & \sin(g_1/2)\\
 2 & G(\phi_*) & \sin(\phi_*/2)\\
 3 & G(\phi_*) & \sin(\phi_*/2),
\end{array}
\]

where `G(t)=(t-sin t)/8`.  The wrapping area floor is the conservative sharp
companion value; using the separate `>0.473` floor requires the narrower Section-107
`sigma<=10^{-3}` window and is not mixed into this calculation.

For these four groups,

\[
\begin{array}{c|c|c|c}
 j & C_{\rm loc}\sqrt{a_j} & \lambda_j
   & (C_{\rm loc}\sqrt{a_j}-\lambda_j)_+\\ \hline
 w & 1.267287374253980 & 0.976243913742569 & 0.291043460511411\\
 1 & 0.974698484607743 & 0.972961137045275 & 0.001737347562468\\
 2 & 0.213661953178687 & 0.423054242362162 & 0\\
 3 & 0.213661953178687 & 0.423054242362162 & 0.
\end{array}
\]

The resulting diameter moment floor is

\[
 S_D/D\ge
 \mu_*+\sin(g_1/2)+2\sin(\phi_*/2)-o(1)
 =2.795313535512168\ldots-o(1).
\tag{GLS.4}
\]

Apply (GLS.3) to the four groups and use nonnegativity for all omitted components:

\[
 3S_D+2G_D
 \ge 8.971502222684261\ldots D-o(D).
\tag{GLS.5}
\]

The retained-remainder payment of normalized Section 161 is

\[
 5h-2d_H-7s_Z
 \ge3S_D+2G_D+c_*D-o(D),
 \qquad
 c_*:=\frac\pi4(2-\sqrt3).
\]

Consequently the new endpoint inequality is

\[
 \boxed{
 5h-2d_H-7s_Z
 \ge9.181949026303494\ldots D-o(D).
 }
\tag{GLS.6}
\]

For comparison, applying the same endpoint moment floor with only the wrapping
carrier's local slack gives `9.178474331178558...`; the large-gap term improves the
coefficient by

\[
 2(0.001737347562468\ldots)
 =0.003474695124936\ldots .
\]

This is a genuine groupwise strengthening, but it is too small and too endpoint-local
to close the positive-detour full-core regime.

## 3. Scope and remaining obligation

- The group area floors use the repaired Section-140 gap-cell saturation and the
  Section-118 sharp-window endpoint profile.  They are not a general Type-II theorem.
- The local aggregate step uses the audited-working local area/slack theorem, not a
  new per-cell convergence assumption.
- The positive part in (GLS.3) prevents an invalid claim that every gap contributes
  positive remainder.
- The four groups are disjoint by the gap-cell convex separation theorem; all omitted
  cells contribute nonnegative `S_D` and `G_D`.
- Contact-isolated source points remain outside all core rigidity matrices.
- No strict-diameter competitor or exact unit equilateral triangle is constructed.

The exact next obligation remains source-level: couple the extra large-gap payment to
the outer-walk detour or to the actual Woodall diameter graph strongly enough to force
a strict diameter decrease.  Type-I inactive containers are untouched.

**Classification:** proved candidate awaiting independent hostile audit; theorem state
unchanged; C-II remains open.
